.TH RTLOG 1 "2026-11-09" "rtlog" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rtlog \- decode rtlog binary log streams to text, JSON lines or Perfetto traces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rtlog decode
.B \-\-contract
.I contract.jsonl
.RB [ \-\-out " " text | json | perfetto ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-color " " auto | always | never ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-spans ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.I stream.rtlog
.br
.B rtlog check
.I contract.jsonl
.br
.B rtlog contract \-\-elf
.I binary
.RB [ \-o
.IR contract.jsonl ]
.br
.B rtlog
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A program that logs with rtlog writes a compact binary stream: a site ID, a
timestamp delta and the raw arguments per call, never the formatted text. The
format strings are in a separate
.IR contract .
.B rtlog
joins the two and prints what the program logged.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B decode
Decode
.I stream.rtlog
with the contract the program wrote
.RB ( rtlog::contract::write ,
or
.B rtlog contract
below). A summary (records, spans, contexts, drops, stream gaps) goes to
standard error. After a damaged frame decoding resumes at the next resync
frame and reports a gap. The exit status is non-zero when decoding stopped
early.
.TP
.B check
Validate a contract and print its number of sites and its hash, the hash the
stream header carries.
.TP
.B contract
Read the site descriptors from an ELF binary (a Linux program or embedded
firmware) and write the contract to standard output or to the
.B \-o
file. Mach-O and PE binaries are not read: on macOS and Windows the program
writes its own contract.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-contract " file"
Contract of the program that wrote the stream.
.TP
.BR \-\-out " text|json|perfetto"
Output format; default text.
.B \-\-json
and
.B \-\-perfetto
are short forms;
.B chrome
is accepted for perfetto. Perfetto output opens in https://ui.perfetto.dev.
.TP
.BI \-o " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-output " file
Write to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " auto|always|never"
Colours in text output. auto: on a terminal, unless
.B NO_COLOR
is set; never with
.BR \-o .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-spans
Leave span open and close records out.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Decode even if the stream's contract hash does not match the contract.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage, also after a command.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, no colours, even on a terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a usage error, an unreadable or invalid file, or a stream
that stopped decoding early.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rtlog decode \-\-contract app.contract.jsonl app.rtlog
rtlog decode \-\-contract app.contract.jsonl \-\-perfetto \-o app.json app.rtlog
rtlog contract \-\-elf firmware.elf \-o firmware.contract.jsonl
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/NieWil/rtlog, docs/reference.md in the source tree.
